{:adr-id "2607152400"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0230 — Gathering of Non-Wood Forest Products Coordination"
 :date "2026-07-14"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC 0230 (Gathering of non-wood forest products -- resin, cork, bark,
  nuts, wild mushrooms, medicinal plants) sat at :spec in kotoba-lang/
  industry's registry with a stale repo reference
  (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0230) that was never published (verified: no
  such repo exists on GitHub). Fresh, from-scratch scaffold, built as
  part of a smaller, carefully verified batch (single agent, capable
  model, mandatory independent re-verification) after an earlier
  18-agent haiku batch's 61% defect rate (empty implementations, missing
  modules, false all-green test claims). Module shape mirrors
  cloud-itonami-isic-0210 (Silviculture and other forestry activities)'s
  own verified redo (ADR-2607142200) -- this fleet's closest domain
  analog (forestry operations coordination) -- domain-adapted for
  non-wood-forest-product gathering (quota-bounded, permit-site-scoped)
  instead of stand/harvest silviculture management."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Back-office coordination-only actor. Closed four-op allowlist, all
   :effect :propose: log-harvest-record (quantity/species/location
   gathering data logging), schedule-field-operation (gathering-trip
   scheduling), flag-sustainability-concern (over-harvest/protected-
   species concern, ALWAYS escalates), order-supplies (equipment/
   permit-fee procurement). Never dispatches field crews, never
   physically gathers a product, never authorizes gathering beyond a
   site's own permitted harvest quota."
  :governor-rules
  "Four HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks (plus unknown-op,
   already-scheduled, invalid-product-category, order-total-mismatch,
   also HARD): (1) not-propose-effect -- the request's own :effect must
   be :propose, evaluated first, unconditional; (2) dispatch-blocked --
   the proposal's own :effect must be one of the closed four
   propose-shaped effects (#{:site/upsert :field-operation/schedule
   :sustainability-concern/flag :supply-order/propose}), anything else
   (a hallucinated :crew/dispatch or :harvest/execute) is the 'direct
   field-crew dispatch' scope violation, permanently blocked; (3)
   site-not-verified -- for schedule-field-operation, the referenced
   site must be independently :verified? in the SSoT before any trip
   may be scheduled against it, never trusted from the advisor's own
   rationale; (4) harvest-quota-exceeded -- for schedule-field-
   operation, independently recompute (from the site's own permanent
   :harvest-quota-kg/:quota-used-kg fields, never the proposal's own
   claimed :quantity-kg) whether the requested gathering would push the
   site's cumulative harvest past its own permitted quota -- ground
   truth, permanent, no override. Escalation (soft): flag-
   sustainability-concern always, order-supplies whose independently-
   recomputed total exceeds the cost threshold (5000.0), low confidence
   (<0.6). nwfp.phase independently agrees -- schedule-field-operation/
   flag-sustainability-concern/order-supplies never auto-commit at any
   phase; only log-harvest-record (no physical/financial risk) may
   auto-commit at phase 3."
  :module-shape
  "nwfp.registry (pure ground-truth-recompute functions: site-verified?,
   harvest-exceeds-quota?, product-category-valid?, order-total(-
   matches-claim?/-exceeds-threshold?), register-field-operation/
   register-supply-order draft construction), nwfp.store (MemStore,
   string-keyed site directory + field-operations + supply-orders +
   sustainability-concerns append-only log + generic records map + audit
   ledger), nwfp.advisor (NwfpAdvisor, mock + real-LLM seam via
   langchain.model), nwfp.governor (NWFP Gathering Coordination
   Governor), nwfp.phase (0->3 rollout), nwfp.operation (langgraph-clj
   StateGraph, NwfpOperationActor), nwfp.sim (demo driver). Module
   set and file layout mirror cloud-itonami-isic-0210's forestry.*
   module-for-module."}
